\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Wayne County has a record from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 49% of normal in August to September and 172% in May to June. So far in 2026 the middle shows 66% for January to February and 76% for May to June. Grid 26019 had its driest year in 1980 at 70% of normal.</p>"}
